\ The sample code the Board tab gives for LED matrices, as generated  ok.
\ (SamplesTest checks that it still matches): a 4-in-1 on SPI3, an 8 x 8 on SPI1.  ok.
#!attach 1 matrix PC9 PC10 PC12 chips=4
#!attach 2 matrix PB10 PB3 PB5 chips=1
  ok.
\ matrix: LED matrix, 4 × MAX7219, 32 × 8, on SPI3: CS PC9, CLK PC10, DIN PC12  ok.
\ Paste all of it into the console, or put it in a file after wiring.fs.  ok.
  ok.
\ PC9 (pin 41) → MAX7219 CS (LOAD); VCC → 5 V, GND → GND  ok.
$48000800 constant matrix-cs-port  \ GPIOC  ok.
9 constant matrix-cs-pin  ok.
\ PC10 (pin 52) → MAX7219 CLK  ok.
$48000800 constant matrix-clk-port  \ GPIOC  ok.
10 constant matrix-clk-pin  ok.
$40003C00 constant matrix-spi  \ SPI3  ok.
6 constant matrix-clk-af  ok.
\ PC12 (pin 54) → MAX7219 DIN, on the module's input end  ok.
$48000800 constant matrix-din-port  \ GPIOC  ok.
12 constant matrix-din-pin  ok.
6 constant matrix-din-af  ok.
  ok.
\ ms: wait n milliseconds, counted by SysTick at 16 MHz  ok.
\ (lib_systick uses SysTick too: with it loaded, use its delay-ms)  ok.
: ms ( n -- )  ok.
  15999 $E000E014 !  0 $E000E018 !  5 $E000E010 ! \ SysTick: wrap every 16000 cycles  ok.
  0 ?do begin $E000E010 @ $10000 and until loop   \ count the wraps  ok.
  0 $E000E010 ! ;                                 \ SysTick off again  ok.
  ok.
: matrix-sr ( -- u ) matrix-spi 8 + @ ;           \ SPI3 SR  ok.
: >matrix ( b -- )                                \ one byte out  ok.
  begin matrix-sr 2 and until  matrix-spi $C + c! ; \ wait for TXE; c! writes one frame  ok.
: matrix-idle ( -- ) begin matrix-sr $80 and 0= until ; \ until BSY clears: the last byte is out  ok.
: matrix-select ( -- ) 1 matrix-cs-pin lshift 16 lshift matrix-cs-port $18 + ! ; \ CS (LOAD) low  ok.
: matrix-load ( -- ) matrix-idle 1 matrix-cs-pin lshift matrix-cs-port $18 + ! ; \ CS high: each chip takes its 16 bits  ok.
: matrix-all ( reg v -- )                         \ the same register in every chip  ok.
  matrix-select  4 0 do over >matrix dup >matrix loop 2drop matrix-load ;  ok.
  ok.
32 buffer: matrix-buf                             \ the picture: 8 rows of 4 bytes, left to right  ok.
: matrix-clear ( -- ) matrix-buf 32 0 fill ;  ok.
: matrix-pixel ( x y -- )                         \ x 0..31 from the left, y 0..7 from the top  ok.
  over 32 u< over 8 u< and 0= if 2drop exit then  ok.
  4 * over 3 rshift + matrix-buf +                \ the byte: row y, column x/8  ok.
  $80 rot 7 and rshift swap cbis! ;               \ bit 7 is the left LED  ok.
: matrix-show ( -- )                              \ the picture to the LEDs, a row at a time  ok.
  8 0 do  ok.
    matrix-select  ok.
    4 0 do  j 1+ >matrix  j 4 * i + matrix-buf + c@ >matrix  loop \ register: row + 1; the left chip first  ok.
    matrix-load  ok.
  loop ;  ok.
  ok.
: matrix-init ( -- )  ok.
  1 2 lshift $4002104C bis!                       \ RCC AHB2ENR: clock for GPIOC  ok.
  1 15 lshift $40021058 bis!                      \ RCC APB1ENR1: clock for SPI3  ok.
  1 15 lshift $40021038 2dup bis! bic!            \ RCC APB1RSTR1: reset SPI3, nothing left in it from another part  ok.
  1 matrix-cs-pin lshift matrix-cs-port $18 + !   \ BSRR: high before it becomes an output  ok.
  %11 matrix-cs-pin 2* lshift matrix-cs-port bic! \ MODER: clear the two bits  ok.
  %01 matrix-cs-pin 2* lshift matrix-cs-port bis! \ MODER: 01 = output  ok.
  1 matrix-cs-pin lshift matrix-cs-port 4 + bic!  \ OTYPER: push-pull  ok.
  %11 matrix-clk-pin 2* lshift matrix-clk-port bic! \ MODER: clear the two bits  ok.
  %10 matrix-clk-pin 2* lshift matrix-clk-port bis! \ MODER: 10 = alternate function  ok.
  1 matrix-clk-pin lshift matrix-clk-port 4 + bic! \ OTYPER: push-pull  ok.
  $F matrix-clk-pin 8 - 4 * lshift matrix-clk-port $24 + bic! \ AFRH: clear the four bits  ok.
  matrix-clk-af matrix-clk-pin 8 - 4 * lshift matrix-clk-port $24 + bis! \ AFRH: AF6 = SPI3 SCK  ok.
  %11 matrix-din-pin 2* lshift matrix-din-port bic! \ MODER: clear the two bits  ok.
  %10 matrix-din-pin 2* lshift matrix-din-port bis! \ MODER: 10 = alternate function  ok.
  1 matrix-din-pin lshift matrix-din-port 4 + bic! \ OTYPER: push-pull  ok.
  $F matrix-din-pin 8 - 4 * lshift matrix-din-port $24 + bic! \ AFRH: clear the four bits  ok.
  matrix-din-af matrix-din-pin 8 - 4 * lshift matrix-din-port $24 + bis! \ AFRH: AF6 = SPI3 MOSI  ok.
  $1700 matrix-spi 4 + !                          \ CR2: 8-bit frames  ok.
  $354 matrix-spi !                               \ CR1: master, SCK = 16 MHz / 8 (it takes 10 MHz), SSM and SSI, on  ok.
  $F 0 matrix-all                                 \ display test off  ok.
  9 0 matrix-all                                  \ no decoding: each bit is an LED  ok.
  $B 7 matrix-all                                 \ scan all 8 rows: after power-up only row 0 shows  ok.
  $A 3 matrix-all                                 \ intensity 3 of 15  ok.
  matrix-clear matrix-show                        \ its rows hold noise at power-up  ok.
  $C 1 matrix-all ;                               \ out of shutdown: on  ok.
  ok.
\ A dot bouncing about until a key is pressed  ok.
0 variable matrix-x  0 variable matrix-y  1 variable matrix-dx  1 variable matrix-dy  ok.
: matrix-move ( -- )  ok.
  matrix-dx @ matrix-x +!  matrix-x @ 0= matrix-x @ 31 = or if matrix-dx @ negate matrix-dx ! then  ok.
  matrix-dy @ matrix-y +!  matrix-y @ 0= matrix-y @ 7 = or if matrix-dy @ negate matrix-dy ! then ;  ok.
: matrix-demo ( -- )  ok.
  matrix-init  ok.
  begin matrix-clear matrix-x @ matrix-y @ matrix-pixel matrix-show matrix-move 50 ms key? until ;  ok.
  ok.
\ Try it: matrix-init 3 3 matrix-pixel matrix-show   or   matrix-demo (Enter stops it)  ok.
  ok.
